<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The wire contract, and nothing else. Generated from proto/parley.proto by Grpc.Tools; this
    project contains no hand-written code at all.

    Separate from the host so that a client can reference it without acquiring a web server.
    Parley.Mcp speaks MCP over stdio and Parley.Cli is a console tool; neither has any business
    carrying Kestrel, and the split is what stops them.

    GrpcServices=Both emits the client stubs and the server base classes into one assembly. They
    are two views of the same contract, and generating them separately would create the
    possibility of a client and a server built from different revisions of it.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <Protobuf Include="..\..\proto\parley.proto" GrpcServices="Both" Link="parley.proto" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Google.Protobuf" />
    <PackageReference Include="Grpc.Net.Client" />
    <PackageReference Include="Grpc.Tools" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Every rule the rest of the repository enforces is aimed at code somebody wrote. Nothing here
    was written, so each of these would be enforcing a convention against protoc's output rather
    than against a decision anyone made.

    CS1591 is the one that matters. Documentation is enforced in Directory.Build.props on the
    argument that the reasoning behind a choice cannot be recovered from the code — and protoc's
    output embodies no choices. The choices are in the .proto, which is commented, and that file
    is the one a reader should be sent to. Silencing the warning here does not weaken the rule
    anywhere it applies.

    Scoped to this project rather than added to the global NoWarn, so a hand-written file that
    appears here later is the signal to reconsider it. There is currently no such file, and the
    absence is deliberate: an assembly that is entirely generated can be regenerated.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CA1707;CA1819;CA2227;CA1062;IDE0005;IDE0058;CA1305;CA1310</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
